sentences.l:
So he spoke, and Alcimedon, onto the aiding chariot having leapt,
swiftly the whip and the reins took in his hands,
and Automedon leapt down;

for forward he bent down, and that, from behind, spear, long,
in the ground was fixed, and upon it the butt-end was shaken
of the spear;

And now indeed with swords at close quarters the two would have rushed at each other,
if the two Ajaxes had not parted the two of them, eager,
who came through the throng as their companion called;

And back again over Patroclus was stretched strong battle,
grievous, of many tears, and was rousing the quarrel Athena,
from heaven having come down;
